  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] (f : E → ℝ),\n  Differentiable ℝ f →\n    ∀ (eta beta lam : ℝ),\n      0 < eta →\n        ∀ (hbeta : 0 ≤ beta),\n          0 ≤ lam →\n            LipschitzWith ⟨beta, hbeta⟩ (gradient f) →\n              ∀ (h xp : E) (r : ℝ),\n                ‖h - xp‖ ≤ √(↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * eta) →\n                  12 * beta ^ 2 * eta ^ 2 * lam ^ 2 ≤ 1 →\n                    have mu :=\n                      (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => h + √eta • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)).prod\n                        (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => √eta • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E));\n                    have F := fun p =>\n                      Real.exp\n                        (lam *\n                          |Inner.inner ℝ\n                              ((Real.pi / 2) •\n                                (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * r) • (p.1 - h) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * r) • p.2))\n                              (gradient f xp -\n                                gradient f\n                                  (h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * r) • (p.1 - h) + Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * r) • p.2))|);\n                    (∀ (x : E), HasGradientAt f (gradient f x) x) ∧\n                      Measurable F ∧\n                        MeasureTheory.Integrable F mu ∧\n                          ∫ (p : E × E), F p ∂mu ≤\n                              2 * Real.exp (10 * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * eta ^ 2 * lam ^ 2 * beta ^ 2) ∧\n                            Real.log (∫ (p : E × E), F p ∂mu) ≤\n                              Real.log 2 + 10 * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * eta ^ 2 * lam ^ 2 * beta ^ 2",
    "statement_sha256": "e97812dcc3fb6addb12e9bcd8ccde818865ad47b5e757211f983127ddb868dbd",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "stdGaussian E is the probability measure of a centered isotropic Gaussian vector with identity covariance on a finite-dimensional real inner product space E. Measure.map is actual pushforward and Measure.prod is independent product.",
      "gradient f is the real inner-product gradient operator; Differentiable means differentiable at every point, and HasGradientAt identifies the derivative through the inner product. LipschitzWith beta means distance of outputs is at most beta times distance of inputs.",
      "Module.finrank is the finite real dimension. Real.sqrt is the nonnegative square root. Integrable is Bochner integrability; the integral and logarithm in the conclusion are real-valued.",
      "All local semantic definitions have been expanded from the compiled theorem type, with definitional equality checked by Lean."
    ]
  },
